# The pidp1.config settings, for pdp1central's settings editor.
# One setting per line: name|group|type|range|default|reader|applies|summary
# type: bool, int, float, text, or port (an int, or off).
# range: low..high, or empty for none.
# default: what the reader uses when the file has no line for the setting; - when there is no
#   single value.
# applies: when a change takes effect. reload is a SIGHUP to pdp1, panel a SIGHUP to the panel
#   driver, restart a pdp1 restart, program a restart of the reader, none never.
#   -sticky: the reader assigns the setting only when a line is there, so a new value applies as
#   stated but going back to the default needs a restart.
# Docs/UsingTheConfigFile.md describes each setting; pidp1.config.example explains it.
ad1port|Debugger|port|0..65535|1044|pdp1|restart|The loopback port ad1 and fastload connect to; 0 or off disables it
ad1remoteport|Debugger|port|0..65535|off|pdp1|restart|A port on all interfaces as well; it has no authentication, so enable it only on a network you trust
throttleburst|Throttle|int|0..250|100|pdp1|reload|How far, in microseconds, simulated time must lead the wall clock before the throttle waits
throttlequantum|Throttle|int|0..1000000|1000|pdp1|reload|The longest single wait, in microseconds
throttlespin|Throttle|int|0..1000000|0|pdp1|reload|The end of each wait, in microseconds, spent spinning instead of sleeping
throttlemaxlag|Throttle|int|0..1000000|20|pdp1|reload|How far, in milliseconds, the emulator may fall behind before the rest is forgiven
lailia|CPU|bool||off|pdp1|reload|The PDP-1D lai and lia instructions, and lsw/swp; always on while core1D or all1D is on
core1D|CPU|bool||on|pdp1|reload|The core PDP-1D extensions; always on while all1D is on
all1D|CPU|bool||off|pdp1|reload|All the PDP-1D extensions
muldiv|CPU|bool||on|pdp1|reload|Hardware multiply and divide
sbs16|CPU|bool||off|pdp1|reload|The 16-channel sequence break system
newmemfile|CPU|bool||off|pdp1|reload|Save memory images in the newer, readable format
sdb|Displays|bool||off|IOT_7|restart|The Type 33 symbol generator's extended dpy
dpyshift|Displays|bool||off|IOT_7|restart|The origin-shifting extended dpy; can conflict with sdb
twoscreens|Displays|bool||off|IOT_7|restart|Dual Type 30 screens, untested
lightpen|Displays|bool||off|IOT_7, IOT_27|restart|Lightpen support on the Type 30 and the Type 33
motionPrediction|Displays|bool||off|pdp1|reload-sticky|Predict the lightpen's motion
aperture|Displays|int|1..63|6|pdp1, IOT_7|restart|The lightpen's aperture, for the Type 340 and the Type 30; 22 is 0.200 inches
two340charsets|Displays|bool||off|Type 340 plugin|reload-sticky|Lower-shift characters from a second character set
t340cachesize|Displays|int|0..1024|0|Type 340 plugin|restart|A Type 340 instruction cache, up to 1024 instructions; 0 for none
guilightpen|Displays|bool||off|pdp1_periph|program|The lightpen in the unified control gui
audio|Audio|bool||off|pdp1|reload|Allow audio; pdp1audio still turns it on
cutoff|Audio|float|1.0..100000.0|-|pdp1|reload|The low-pass cutoff of all four program flag channels, in Hz; without it each has the CHM filter's own
cutoff1|Audio|float|1.0..100000.0|-|pdp1|reload|Program flag 1's cutoff in Hz, overriding cutoff; the CHM filter's is about 1020
cutoff2|Audio|float|1.0..100000.0|-|pdp1|reload|Program flag 2's cutoff in Hz, overriding cutoff; the CHM filter's is about 925
cutoff3|Audio|float|1.0..100000.0|-|pdp1|reload|Program flag 3's cutoff in Hz, overriding cutoff; the CHM filter's is about 423
cutoff4|Audio|float|1.0..100000.0|-|pdp1|reload|Program flag 4's cutoff in Hz, overriding cutoff; the CHM filter's is about 220
gain|Audio|float|0.0..100.0|0.95|pdp1|reload|The mixer gain; too high and the sound clips
tuning|Audio|float|0.001..100.0|1.0|pdp1|reload|Shifts the frequency; SDL3 only
samplerate|Audio|int|8000..192000|48000|pdp1|reload|Samples a second sent to SDL
audiodepth|Audio|int|10..500|40|pdp1|reload|Milliseconds of sound kept queued ahead of the device
fasttyo|Devices|bool||off|IOT_3|restart|Typewriter output at 200 characters a second instead of 10
lptType64|Devices|bool||off|IOT_45|restart|A Type 64 line printer instead of a Type 62
lptLineSpacing|Devices|text||-|IOT_45|restart|Lines advanced for each spacing setting 0-7, comma separated with no spaces, such as 1,2,3,4,11,22,33,-1
lptLines|Devices|int|1..1000|66|IOT_45|restart|Lines per page
lptNoFF|Devices|bool||off|IOT_45|restart|Newlines instead of a form feed character
microtapesbs|Devices|int|0..15|2|Microtape plugin|reload|The Type 550 microtape's sequence break channel
panelbrightness|Panel|int|0..100|100|newpanel|panel-sticky|The brightness cap of the hardware panel's lamps
panelonalpha|Panel|float|0.0..1.0|0.45|newpanel|panel-sticky|The lamps' turn-on rate
paneloffalpha|Panel|float|0.0..1.0|0.04|newpanel|panel-sticky|The lamps' turn-off rate
panelrealtime|Panel|bool||off|newpanel|restart|Realtime priority for the panel driver
panellevels|Panel|int|8..64|8|newpanel|panel-sticky|Brightness levels
panelcycletime|Panel|int|100..1000000|1000|newpanel|panel-sticky|How often the lamp brightnesses are recomputed, in microseconds
panelscantime|Panel|int|100..1000000|1000|newpanel|panel-sticky|The time to scan one row of lamps, in microseconds
pidp1timing|Timing|bool||off|pdp1|reload-sticky|Append the emulator's timing to /tmp/pidp1-timing.txt at each stop
displaytiming|Timing|bool||off|pdp1, Type 340 plugin|restart|Append the display threads' timing to /tmp/pidp1-340timing.txt and /tmp/pidp1-dpytiming.txt
type30lightpen|Retired|bool||off|p7sim|none|The lightpen in the standalone Type 30 display, p7sim, which is no longer in this tree
type30size|Retired|int|512..1024|1024|p7sim|none|The size of the standalone Type 30 display, p7sim, which is no longer in this tree
type30border|Retired|bool||on|p7sim|none|The border of the standalone Type 30 display, p7sim, which is no longer in this tree
shared|Retired|bool||off|pdp1|none|Ignored, with a message; ad1 and fastload reach the emulator over TCP
alpha|Retired|float||-|pdp1|none|Ignored, with a message; the audio filters are set by cutoff, in Hz
alpha1|Retired|float||-|pdp1|none|Ignored, with a message; the audio filters are set by cutoff, in Hz
alpha2|Retired|float||-|pdp1|none|Ignored, with a message; the audio filters are set by cutoff, in Hz
alpha3|Retired|float||-|pdp1|none|Ignored, with a message; the audio filters are set by cutoff, in Hz
alpha4|Retired|float||-|pdp1|none|Ignored, with a message; the audio filters are set by cutoff, in Hz
